# UI

- Whimsical light-first (+ soft dark); **Grandstander** + **Lexend**; Sage Garden tokens from `packages/ui` theme (cream / sage / potato gold — **never** purple/indigo clones).
- **Token roles** (`packages/ui/src/theme.css` + `tailwind-preset`):
  - **primary** = sage — main actions, path, board chrome
  - **secondary** = potato gold — warm brand accent (score badge, selected mode cards, secondary buttons, hard challenge)
  - **accent** = soft sage — hover/soft wash only (not a second brand)
  - **muted** = soft sage-gray — chip/segment tracks, ghost hover
  - Prefer `bg-secondary` / `text-secondary` / `text-secondary-foreground`; `--potato` is an alias of secondary (legacy)
- **UI inspiration (steal craft, keep brand):**
  - [TypeUI](https://www.typeui.sh/) thinking: design-system tokens first, then hierarchy / spacing rhythm / type leading / interaction feedback as the reasoning layer. Steep display→label contrast; motion for entrance, feedback, transition only; depth via luminance + surface — not flat robot UI.
  - Tactile word-game refs (user CleanShot set): pillow cream tiles, thick rounded board frame, circular select (square) / hex tile tint + drop-shadow ring (Honeycomb) + juicy path stroke, word pill + score badge, atmospheric background. No Scrabble TW/TL multipliers. Hex select is the clipped tile itself (`HEX_CLIP`) so `--cp-tile-gap` gutters cannot offset a separate overlay; path SVG shares `.cp-board-play` with the tile grid.
- **Motion:** any meaningful interactivity should show the change — short CSS/NativeWind transitions/feedback (segment pill slide, select pop, Goal↔Timed swap, button press, path/score ticks, screen enter). Keep whimsical, light, performant. Prefer CSS; don’t animate everything mindlessly; honor `prefers-reduced-motion`. No anime.js unless CSS can’t cover it.
- **Accordions / collapsibles:** always animate open/close (height via CSS grid `0fr`→`1fr`, opacity, chevron rotate). Prefer that pattern (or shadcn `Collapsible` if already in tree) over raw `<details>` with an instant snap. Instant open/close only under `prefers-reduced-motion`. Lobby **Min length** is always-visible choice cards (same `.cp-lobby-challenge` pattern as How hard?), not an accordion.
- **Web chrome:** shadcn/ui (Radix + Tailwind) is the preferred base for Button/input/dialog/toast — customize (toy press shadows), don’t hand-roll duplicates. Game board (`LetterGrid`, path, tile drop, confetti) stays custom + tactile. Board cast shadow lives on non-rotating `.cp-board-frame`; only `.cp-board-spin` rotates (see `AGENTS.md` Rotate).
- **Copy / voice:** prefer **gaming terminology** (Play, lobby, run, haul, SFX, spin, Couch crew) over sterile app/form words (Submit, Settings, Confirm). Whimsical Couch Potato: clear for casual players, not esports jargon. **Never use em dashes (—)** in player-facing copy (UI strings, toasts, tooltips/`aria-label`, share text, SEO titles/descriptions); prefer comma, period, or a hyphen sparingly. Icon tooltips/`aria-label` match that voice.
- **Prefer icons** for controls/options when the glyph is faster (sound, pause, rotate, couch crew, share; lobby chips): `lucide-react` + `aria-label` + shadcn `IconTooltip` (hover/focus; Radix long-press on touch — don’t rely on tooltip alone). Drop native `title` when Tooltip is present (double chrome). Keep lobby mode/challenge labeled; mid-run **End run** lives in the Escape/pause menu (soft confirm). Lobby options get lucide glyphs + `.cp-lobby-glyph` hover/press juice. Lobby **section titles** get a muted decorative lucide icon beside the label (same size/weight as Show words left eye); mode cards keep their own glyphs.
- **Active / selected / on states must be obvious** (color + ring + weight), not a subtle border-only change. Selected lobby glyphs use potato `text-secondary` (or `text-secondary-foreground` on a secondary wash like Hard / Words left on); inactive stay `text-muted-foreground`. Soft lucide fill (`fillOpacity` ~0.22) amps selected. Don’t use `text-primary` alone for “on” on cream: sage primary ≈ muted-foreground and reads as still-off.
- **Icon-only motion:** Button `size="icon"` / `icon-sm` → shared `.cp-icon-btn` (hover lift + scale ~1.12 + potato/secondary tint, active squash, `aria-pressed` potato ring + pulse). **Pref toggles** (jam/SFX): `variant="outline"` off (muted border/fill), `aria-pressed="true"` potato wash + ring — not filled `secondary` CTAs. CSS only; honor `prefers-reduced-motion`. `aria-pressed` = feature **on**, not muted. Icon tooltips: feature + state (`SFX on` / `Lobby jam off`). **Jam icons:** `Music2` on, local `MusicOff` off (not Volume; those are SFX).
- **Couch break prefs:** shadcn `Switch` rows — fixed labels (`SFX`, `Lobby jam`, `Show words left`); checked = potato `secondary` track + warm row wash. Don’t encode state in the label text. Lobby Show words left matches (Switch + helper: during play, running count of words still to find).
- **Web cursors:** lean global rule in `apps/web/src/index.css` (`button`, `[role=button]`, `a[href]`, `summary`, labels/inputs) — don’t sprinkle `cursor-pointer` per class. Letter board: `grab` / `grabbing` while swiping. Tile hit acceptance uses `--cp-tile-gap` gutters + `isInTileHitZone` edge inset (dead zone between letters). Path backtrack (revisit → pop/truncate) only in the tile **center zone** (`isInBacktrackZone` / `allowBacktrack`) so diagonal transit that clips a previous corner does not false-pop.
- `packages/ui` RN Button = Expo/RN path; web app chrome → shadcn. Don’t maintain two competing web Buttons.
- Mobile-first; minimize one-off Tailwind in routes.
- **Home lobby IA:** toy cards/tiles (`HomeSetup`) — not stacked MODE/GRID label+segment rows. **Primary** (what am I playing): mode → board → challenge. **Advanced** (fine-tune, quieter): min length → Show words left. Phone: single stack primary then advanced. Wide web (container ≥36rem): primary left | advanced right; cards hug content (`align-items: start`, no stretch). Sticky Play outside scroller; on md+ lobby, Play + jam/SFX cluster max ~28rem centered (phone stays full-width dominant Play).
- **Home lobby width (web):** Shell default stays `max-w-md` (play/results). Lobby Home adds `cp-shell-lobby` (wider at md/lg/xl in `apps/web` `index.css`) + `@container lobby` on `.cp-lobby`: brand = logo + wordmark hero, full tagline under title (wide = logo | stacked copy). Cross-platform flex + max-width; no `@container` in RN.
- **Play HUD IA:** one top row — primary status (`N pts` remaining for Goal, or timer for timed) + compact icon cluster (mute / pause only); words-left count as muted “N left” readout when on (toggle lives in Couch break + lobby — not HUD); no stacked haul/score pills (per-word pts live on the word-bubble badge); progress under the row for Goal; spin stays by the board. Primary pill **heats** with progress (muted → sage/`path` → potato `secondary`): Goal = `1 − remaining/target`, timed = `score/maxScore`; brief pulse on clear/haul (`prefers-reduced-motion` → color only).
- **Container queries = web-only.** Cross-platform layout: flex + max-width. No `@container` in pure RN views.
- **Viewport shells:** root `h-dvh overflow-hidden` → `Shell` fills height (`flex flex-col min-h-0`). Scroll inside a child (`flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto cp-shell-scroll`), not body alone — lobby keeps Play+mute as a shrink-0 footer outside that scroller; `.cp-lobby-play` owns bottom safe-area + shadow room (`padding-bottom: max(1.25rem, calc(1rem + env(safe-area-inset-bottom)))`). Lobby Shell: no `overflow-hidden`/`pb-0` on the column (clips the bar). Web: `.cp-shell-scroll` in `packages/ui` `theme.css` = `scrollbar-gutter: stable` + thin thumb + right inset so overlay bars don’t clip cards.
- UI changes require interactive verify (pointer swipe for play) — see `.cursor/skills/verify-ui`.
